# The platform's masters for the kernel's controllers (foldsim_storage
# platform_cost 'best', the FOLDSIM_VMEM_MASTERS the flow sets): by the whole
# HBM share (HBM_BYTES_PER_CYCLE: 10 beats a host cycle, 10 masters, 3
# sc_mem nodes past the 8 HBM ports) or, with a point's own traffic
# (foldsim_degree state --masters-by-traffic), its beats x MASTER_HEADROOM:
# a light 128-SM point (35 bytes a host cycle) takes 7 (8 masters with the
# folded port's: no sc_mem node), never more than the share's (480 bytes).
# RUN: python3 %S/Inputs/platform/masters.py foldsim | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: ctl 13 traffic None: vmem masters 10 masters 11 shares 10 sc_nodes 3 luts 28764
# CHECK: ctl 13 traffic 35.3: vmem masters 7 masters 8 shares 7 sc_nodes 0 luts 8484
# CHECK: ctl 13 traffic 480.0: vmem masters 10 masters 11 shares 10 sc_nodes 3 luts 28764
# CHECK: ctl 84 traffic None: vmem masters 10 masters 11 shares 10 sc_nodes 3 luts 99835
# CHECK: ctl 84 traffic 72.2: vmem masters 7 masters 8 shares 7 sc_nodes 0 luts 79555
